    "pressure": {
      "file": "shaft_alignment_system_pressure.glb",
      "title": "Offset and angularity — measure, then correct",
      "description": "Two shafts are aligned when their rotational centrelines are collinear at running temperature. Misalignment has two parts: offset (parallel displacement) and angularity (slope), each vertical and horizontal. With the bracket on one hub, rotating both shafts together and reading the rim (radial) and face (axial) indicators at 12, 3, 6 and 9 o'clock gives offset (½ the rim reading change) and angularity (face difference ÷ diameter). Correct vertical errors with shims under the movable machine's feet, horizontal with jacking bolts; check soft foot first. Typical tolerances at 1500 rpm ≈ 0.05–0.08 mm offset (follow site / maker tables).",
      "render": "normal",
      "annotations": []
    }
  },
